<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>governauthzer API — v1</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <style>body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }</style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <redoc spec-url="<%= api_docs_spec_path %>"></redoc>
    <%# Redoc 2.5.4, vendored (vendor/javascript/redoc.standalone.js, MIT). Served from
        this origin, not a CDN: a script from elsewhere runs with the operator session's
        origin, and an internal network may have no route to the CDN at all. Pinned to
        2.x on purpose — 3.x sends usage telemetry to Redocly by default and loads its
        icons from their CDN. To upgrade, replace the file from the npm tarball after
        checking its `dist.integrity`. %>
    <%= javascript_include_tag "redoc.standalone" %>
  </body>
</html>
